; The container `for` over something that is not a container.
;
; This case PARSES - `(for x in n body)` is a well-formed three-element
; `for` - and is refused by the checker at the user's OWN expression:
; a declared container's expression is underlined. A declared non-Vec
; draws two rows: the desugaring reads its length and then its elements.
; Their spans identify the user's expression and the `for` keyword.
; A parameter without a signature has no declared container type. Its
; default Int is poisoned after the first mismatch, so the definition
; draws one AX3089 asking for the signature. Other definitions and
; independent mistakes keep their own diagnostics.
;
;   1  a DECLARED `Int` parameter. `expected Vec _a, found Int`.
;   2  an undeclared parameter, which defaults to `Int`.
;      The definition draws one AX3089; a `(Vec a)` signature makes
;      the loop checkable. The declared Int case above keeps its two
;      errors for its two invalid container reads.
;   3  a `String`. `for` iterates `(Vec a)` directly, so the rows name
;      the bytes idiom instead: `(for i in 0..(strLen s) ... (strByte s i)
;      ...)`.
;   4  a `Map`. Same shape, the keys idiom: `(for k in (mapKeys m) ...
;      (mapGet m k default) ...)`.
;
; The file declares its OWN `vecLen`. That is the ablation this case
; exists to hold: the desugaring emits the MANGLED `Vec$vecLen` and
; `Vec$vecGet`, the spelling `mangledFromChain` gives `Vec::vecLen`, so
; a name the entry file declares cannot capture it. Emit a bare
; `vecLen` instead and this file's own wins - the messages become
; `expected Vec Int` and the case goes red. MAC-CAP-10.5 records the
; same defect being real once: an entry file's own `concat` captured
; the format lowering's, silently and wrongly.
(import IO)
(import Map)

(:: vecLen (-> (Vec Int) Int))
(fn (vecLen z)
  99)

(:: overAnInt (-> Int Int))
;@axiom:effect(io)
(fn (overAnInt n)
  (for x in n
    (println 1)))

;@axiom:effect(io)
(fn (overAnUndeclaredParam xs)
  (for x in xs
    (println 1)))

(:: overAString (-> String Int))
;@axiom:effect(io)
(fn (overAString s)
  (for c in s
    (println 1)))

(:: overAMap (-> (Map Int Int) Int))
;@axiom:effect(io)
(fn (overAMap m)
  (for k in m
    (println 1)))

(:: main ())
(fn (main)
  ())
